🌾 AI-Powered Crop Recommendation System
Abstract
Agriculture plays a vital role in the economy, and selecting the right crop based on soil and environmental conditions is essential for improving productivity. This project presents an AI-Powered Crop Recommendation System that predicts the most suitable crop using machine learning techniques. The system analyzes soil nutrients (Nitrogen, Phosphorus, and Potassium) along with environmental parameters such as temperature, humidity, pH, and rainfall to recommend an appropriate crop.
The application is developed using a Flask backend, an interactive web frontend, and a Gaussian Naive Bayes machine learning model trained on a crop recommendation dataset. Prediction history is stored and analyzed using Apache Spark to generate useful agricultural insights. Apache Hive integration is planned for large-scale data storage and querying. This project demonstrates the integration of Artificial Intelligence and Big Data technologies in a practical agricultural application.
1. Introduction
Agriculture is one of the most important sectors contributing to food production and economic growth. Farmers often face challenges in selecting suitable crops due to varying soil conditions, climatic changes, and lack of timely information. Incorrect crop selection can result in reduced yield and financial losses.
Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Machine Learning (ML) provide an effective solution by analyzing historical agricultural data and recommending crops based on multiple environmental factors. This project combines Machine Learning with Big Data technologies to create a system capable of providing intelligent crop recommendations while maintaining prediction history for analytical purposes.
The system is designed to be user-friendly, allowing users to enter soil and weather parameters through a web interface and receive instant crop recommendations.
2. Problem Statement
Farmers often rely on traditional knowledge and experience when selecting crops. However, environmental conditions such as soil nutrients, rainfall, temperature, humidity, and pH significantly affect crop growth. Manual decision-making may not always produce the best results.
There is a need for an intelligent system that can analyze these parameters and recommend the most suitable crop while maintaining historical prediction data for future analysis.
3. Objectives
The main objectives of this project are:
- To develop a machine learning model capable of recommending suitable crops.
- To build a web-based application for crop prediction.
- To integrate the trained model with a Flask backend.
- To store prediction history for future analysis.
- To perform analytical processing using Apache Spark.
- To integrate Apache Hive for Big Data storage and querying.
- To provide a simple and user-friendly interface for users.
